-- title:
--   Uniform bound for sampled kernel outputs
-- statement:
--   For a box radius $M$ and constants $C_B,C_C,L\ge0$, the output bound is
--   $$
--   \mathrm{outputBound}(M,C_B,C_C,L)=\int_{\mathbb R}\mathbf 1_{[-(M+1),M+1]}(c)\,C_BC_CL\,dc=2(M+1)\,C_BC_CL .
--   $$
--   If $|B|\le C_B$ and $|C|\le C_C$ are supported in the box of radius $M$ (enlarged by the grid mesh), and the kernel is bounded by $L$, then every sampled cyclic kernel output $\int B(\cdot,c)C(c,\cdot)K(\cdot)\,dc$ is bounded by this constant. This gives a uniform bound needed for dominated convergence as the mesh tends to zero.
